  <paragraph>We have now seen two methods you can use to multiply a trinomial by a binomial. After you practice each method, you’ll probably find you prefer one way over the other. We list both methods are listed here, for easy reference.</paragraph>
  <note type="rule" source_type="Multiplying a Trinomial by a Binomial" title="Multiplying a Trinomial by a Binomial">
    <paragraph>To multiply a trinomial by a binomial, use the:</paragraph>
    <list type="unordered">
      <item>Distributive Property</item>
      <item>Vertical Method</item>
    </list>
  </note>
